  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-213462",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First of all, notice that $\\text{gcd}(75,22)=1.$ So, the multiplicative inverse of $22$ modulo $75$ exists.\n\nThe multiplicative inverse of $22$ modulo $75$ is the number $x$ such that\n\n$$\n22\\cdot x≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,75).\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $x,$ we will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}75 & = & 22\\cdot 3 & + & 9 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 22 & = & 9\\cdot 2 & + & 4 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 9 & = & 4\\cdot 2 & + & 1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSolving for the rightmost terms in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9 & =75-22\\cdot 3 \\\\ 4 & =22-9\\cdot 2 \\\\ 1 & =9-4\\cdot 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =9-4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =9-(22-9\\cdot 2)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =9-22\\cdot 2+9\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =9\\cdot 5-22\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =(75-22\\cdot 3)\\cdot 5-22\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =75\\cdot 5-22\\cdot 15-22\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =75\\cdot 5-22\\cdot 17 \\\\  & =22\\cdot (-17)+75\\cdot (5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can write this result modulo $75,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}22\\cdot (-17)+75\\cdot 5 & ≡1 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,75) \\\\ 22\\cdot (-17) & ≡1 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,75) \\\\ 22\\cdot (75-17) & ≡1 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,75) \\\\ 22\\cdot 58 & ≡1 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,75)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $22\\cdot 58≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,75),$ which means that ${22}^{-1}\\,\\text{mod}\\,75=58.$",
